\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Lift up your heads ye mighty gates,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Behold the King of glory waits!
\par The King of Kings is drawing near,
\par The Saviour of the world is here:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Life and salvation doth He bring.
\par Wherefore rejoice and gladly sing.
\par We praise Thee Father, now
\par Creator, wise art Thou!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   The Lord is just, a helper tried,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Mercy is ever at His side;
\par His Kingly crown is holiness
\par His sceptre, pity in distress;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The end of all our woe He brings,
\par Wherefore the earth is glad and sings,
\par We praise Thee, Saviour, now
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Mighty in deed art Thou!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   O blest the land, the city blest.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Where Christ the ruler is confest!
\par O happy hearts and happy homes
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj To whom this King in triumph comes!
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The cloudless sun of joy He is,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   Who bringeth pure delight and bliss
\par   O Comforter Divine,
\par   hat boundless grace is Thine!
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fling wide the portals of your heart
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj  Make it a temple set apart
\par  From earthly use, for heaven's employ,
\par   Adorned with prayer, and love and joy:
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj So shall your Sovereign enter in.
\par   And new and nobler life begin.
\par   To thee, O God, be praise.
\par   For word and deed and grace.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Redeemer, come, we open wide
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   Our heart to Thee: here, Lord, abide!
\par  Thine inner presence let us feel,
\par   Thy grace and love in us reveal,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thy Holy Spirit guide us on,
\par   Until the glorious goal is won
\par  Eternal praise and fame
\par \pard   We offer to Thy name.  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

